Use the wasm object-format section syntax for the ICU data blob on wasm32.

icu_data.S embeds the ICU data with .incbin. Wasm objects need the WASI form:
`.section .rodata,"",@` and an explicit .size for the data symbol.

ESR 153 rebase: icu_data.S is now a template fed through icu_data_hash.py,
which prepends the ICU_DATA_HASH define, and gained an `.ascii ICU_DATA_HASH`
line; only the two __wasi__ conditions change.

--- a/config/external/icu/data/icu_data.S
+++ b/config/external/icu/data/icu_data.S
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 #elif defined(__APPLE__)
 .data
 .const
-#elif defined(__wasi__)
+#elif defined(__wasi__) || defined(__wasm32__)
 .section .rodata,"",@
 #else
 .section .rodata
@@ -27,6 +27,6 @@
 .balign 16
 ICU_DATA_SYMBOL:
 .incbin ICU_DATA_FILE
-#ifdef __wasi__
+#if defined(__wasi__) || defined(__wasm32__)
 .size ICU_DATA_SYMBOL, . - ICU_DATA_SYMBOL
 #endif
